 "capsule": "Having declared independence on 24 February 1918, the Republic of Estonia secured it by defeating Soviet and German-allied forces in the War of Independence (1918-1920) and the Tartu Peace Treaty of February 1920, after which it functioned as a parliamentary democracy under successive State Elders. Political instability during the Depression let Konstantin Päts seize authoritarian power in the 1934 'era of silence' coup, ruling as State Elder and later President; independence ended in June 1940 when the Soviet Union, acting under the Molotov-Ribbentrop Pact, occupied and annexed the country.",
